    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "title",
      "text": "A closer look at life:",
      "font": "Hand",
      "size": 44,
      "bounds": [
        47.76,
        96.50800000000001,
        343.836,
        132.5
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "title",
      "text": "what is inside a cell?",
      "font": "Hand",
      "size": 44,
      "bounds": [
        50.752,
        139.61599999999999,
        365.79200000000003,
        172.968
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "lead",
      "text": "Look at your hand, then at a green leaf by the window. Both are made of cells. Cells",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 16,
      "bounds": [
        49.616,
        210.056,
        663.7919999999997,
        227.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "lead",
      "text": "are the basic units of life, and most are so small that we need a microscope to see",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 16,
      "bounds": [
        48.944,
        233.056,
        651.2639999999999,
        249.664
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "lead",
      "text": "them. Let's enlarge a typical animal cell and see how its parts work together.",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 16,
      "bounds": [
        48.432,
        256.264,
        615.3119999999999,
        273.0
      ]
    },
