        621.182
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "label.Mitochondria",
      "text": "Mitochondria",
      "font": "Heading",
      "size": 13,
      "bounds": [
        601.183,
        432.457,
        680.678,
        443.182
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.0",
      "text": "The cell membrane separates the inside from the outside and controls what moves in and",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        48.465,
        697.865,
        670.56,
        713.435
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.0",
      "text": "out. Between the membrane and the nucleus is the cytoplasm, where many chemical",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        48.78,
        720.06,
        639.855,
        735.51
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.0",
      "text": "reactions take place. The nucleus holds most of the cell's DNA. The genetic information it",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        49.38,
        741.865,
        666.765,
        757.75
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.0",
      "text": "carries helps direct the cell's activities.",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        48.78,
        764.06,
        315.585,
        779.435
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.1",
      "text": "How do those instructions become work? Ribosomes use the messages they receive to",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        49.515,
        798.06,
        648.8549999999997,
        813.75
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.1",
      "text": "make proteins, which help form the cell's structures and carry out many of its activities.",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        49.38,
        819.865,
        655.53,
        835.51
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.1",
      "text": "Mitochondria convert energy from nutrients into forms the cell can use, such as ATP, to",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        49.515,
        841.865,
        651.9899999999997,
        857.75
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
      "id": "paragraph.1",
      "text": "support this work.",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15,
      "bounds": [
        48.48,
        864.06,
        174.21,
        879.435
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 1,
