    {
      "page": 2,
      "id": "closing",
      "text": "Animals and plants are eukaryotes; bacteria are prokaryotes. To begin telling them",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15.5,
      "bounds": [
        48.062,
        792.162,
        641.8514999999998,
        808.375
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "id": "closing",
      "text": "apart, look for a membrane-bound nucleus, then other features such as a cell wall or",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15.5,
      "bounds": [
        48.9145,
        814.9605,
        655.3365,
        831.0495
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "id": "closing",
      "text": "chloroplasts. Their shapes may differ greatly, but all cells do the work that keeps life",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15.5,
      "bounds": [
        48.806,
        837.9605,
        651.5234999999999,
        854.375
      ]
    },
    {
      "page": 2,
      "id": "closing",
      "text": "going.",
      "font": "Body",
      "size": 15.5,
      "bounds": [
        48.7905,
